ed}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3-0)^{2}+(-4-(-4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115360/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e9df1ae-8176-555b-987d-94773c27d435"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115360"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263134/field-1/4d31c9cc5368f8cb8fa2d5661886836ed8f2cebf6125f1b80fa1f903bde9bebe" :answer/id #uuid "b7ca3d72-eb97-56c8-ae38-8b8fd0c6bc28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263134/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1131fbc-fb07-5469-b1f1-34075ac0a0d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263134/field-1/4d31c9cc5368f8cb8fa2d5661886836ed8f2cebf6125f1b80fa1f903bde9bebe" :answer-field/choices ["q-263134/field-1/4d31c9cc5368f8cb8fa2d5661886836ed8f2cebf6125f1b80fa1f903bde9bebe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263134" :question/id #uuid "f7a2172d-47d5-55a4-bfba-9edbee7bffb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-263134" :question/problem "The points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $(-3,-4)$ and $(9,8)$, respectively, and the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter of a circle. Determine the radius $r$ of the circle.\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3-9)^{2}+(-4-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+(-12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{288} \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{12\\sqrt{2}}{2}=6\\sqrt{2}\n$$" :question/difficulty 